# covers: 1 E3.2, 1a 3.7
# 1-social-aggro-a (with 1-social-aggro-b): A attacks one keltir; the clan call (keltir.toml
# clan_id "keltir", clan_help_range 8 tiles) brings the others into the fight. A stands at
# (95, 100): 5 tiles from the keltir_a home (two members, which may aggro A on their own) and
# 9.2 from keltir_b's, outside its aggro range (6 tiles). keltir_b swinging at A, i.e. all three
# keltirs, is the social aggro: keltir_b's home is 4.5 tiles from keltir_a's, inside the call.
# (A keltir_b that wandered within 6 tiles of A would aggro it on its own: the wander drift is up
# to 9.4 tiles per axis around home, 1 think in 30.)
#
# B walks out first (along y = 40) so it is at its post before A fights; A waits until B has left
# its view. Timeouts 3x: walks at 5 tiles/s, aggro on the next 1 s think, swings every ~2 s.
nf.Login
nf.WaitFor connected 15
nf.EnterWorld
nf.WaitFor in_world 15
nf.WaitFor players_in_view >= 1 30
nf.WaitFor players_in_view == 0 60 # B crossed x = 64
nf.ClickMove 40 40
nf.WaitFor own_at 40 40 1 35
nf.ClickMove 80 85
nf.WaitFor own_at 80 85 1 35
nf.ClickMove 95 100
nf.WaitFor own_at 95 100 1 15
nf.Target nearest_attackable
nf.WaitFor target != none 3
nf.Attack
nf.WaitFor attack_state == active 3
nf.WaitFor attacked_by >= 3 15     # all three, keltir_b by the clan call: think 1 s + swing 2 s + a 4-tile walk, 3x
nf.WaitFor target_hp == 0 30
nf.Within 180
